[4.611026, "o", "nmeter (12 kb) (NMETER) [Y/n/?] y\r\npgrep (6.8 kb) (PGREP) [Y/n/?] y\r\npkill (7.8 kb) (PKILL) [Y/n/?] y\r\npidof (6.5 kb) (PIDOF) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable single shot (-s) (FEATURE_PIDOF_SINGLE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable omitting pids (-o PID) (FEATURE_PIDOF_OMIT) [Y/n/?] y\r\npmap (6.2 kb) (PMAP) [Y/n/?] y\r\npowertop (9.9 kb) (POWERTOP) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Accept keyboard commands (FEATURE_POWERTOP_INTERACTIVE) [Y/n/?] y\r\nps (12 kb) (PS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable -o time and -o etime specifiers (FEATURE_PS_TIME) [Y/n] y\r\n    Support Linux prior to 2.4.0 and non-ELF systems (FEATURE_PS_UNUSUAL_SYSTEMS) [N/y/?] n\r\n  Enable -o rgroup, -o ruser, -o nice specifiers (FEATURE_PS_ADDITIONAL_COLUMNS) [Y/n] y\r\npstree (9.4 kb) (PSTREE) [Y/n/?] y\r\npwdx (3.9 kb) (PWDX) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsmemcap (3 kb) (SMEMCAP) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsysctl (7.9 kb) (BB_SYSCTL) [Y/n/?] y\r\ntop (18 kb) (TOP) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Accept keyboard commands (FEATURE_TOP_INTERACTIVE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Show CPU per-process usage percentage (FEATURE_TOP_CPU_USAGE_PERCENTAGE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    Show CPU global usage percentage (FEATURE_TOP_CPU_GLOBAL_PERCENTS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n      SMP CPU usage display ('c' key) (FEATURE_TOP_SMP_CPU) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    Show 1/10th of a percent in CPU/mem statistics (FEATURE_TOP_DECIMALS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Show CPU process runs on ('j' field) (FEATURE_TOP_SMP_PROCESS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Topmem command ('s' key) (FEATURE_TOPMEM) [Y/n/?] y\r\nuptime (4 kb) (UPTIME) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Show the number of users (FEATURE_UPTIME_UTMP_SUPPORT) [Y/n/?] y\r\nvmstat (2 kb) (VMSTAT) [Y/n/?] y\r\nwatch (5.2 kb) (WATCH) [Y/n/?] y\r\n*\r\n* Runit Utilities\r\n*\r\nchpst (9.2 kb) (CHPST) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsetuidgid (4.2 kb) (SETUIDGID) [Y/n/?] y\r\nenvuidgid (4.1 kb) (ENVUIDGID) [Y/n/?] y\r\nenvdir (2.9 kb) (ENVDIR) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsoftlimit (4.7 kb) (SOFTLIMIT) [Y/n/?] y\r\nrunsv (8.2 kb) (RUNSV) [Y/n/?] y\r\nrunsvdir (6.6 kb) (RUNSVDIR) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable scrolling argument log (FEATURE_RUNSVDIR_LOG) [N/y/?] n\r\nsv (8.7 kb) (SV) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Default directory for services (SV_DEFAULT_SERVICE_DIR) [/var/service] /var/service\r\nsvc (8.7 kb) (SVC) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsvok (1.8 kb) (SVOK) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsvlogd (16 kb) (SVLOGD) [Y/n/?] y\r\n*\r\n* Shells\r\n*\r\nChoose which shell is aliased to 'sh' name\r\n"]
[4.611131, "o", "> 1. ash (SH_IS_ASH)\r\n  2. hush (SH_IS_HUSH)\r\n"]
[4.611205, "o", "  3. none (SH_IS_NONE)\r\nchoice[1-3?]: 1\r\nChoose which shell is aliased to 'bash' name\r\n  1. ash (BASH_IS_ASH)\r\n  2. hush (BASH_IS_HUSH)\r\n> 3. none (BASH_IS_NONE)\r\nchoice[1-3?]: 3\r\nash (80 kb) (ASH) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Optimize for size instead of speed (ASH_OPTIMIZE_FOR_SIZE) [Y/n] y\r\n"]
[4.611249, "o", "  Use internal glob() implementation (ASH_INTERNAL_GLOB) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  bash-compatible extensions (ASH_BASH_COMPAT) [Y/n] y\r\n"]
[4.61133, "o", "    'source' and '.' builtins search current directory after $PATH (ASH_BASH_SOURCE_CURDIR) [N/y/?] n\r\n    command_not_found_handle hook support (ASH_BASH_NOT_FOUND_HOOK) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Job control (ASH_JOB_CONTROL) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Alias support (ASH_ALIAS) [Y/n] y\r\n"]
[4.611371, "o", "  Pseudorandom generator and $RANDOM variable (ASH_RANDOM_SUPPORT) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Expand prompt string (ASH_EXPAND_PRMT) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Idle timeout variable $TMOUT (ASH_IDLE_TIMEOUT) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Check for new mail in interactive shell (ASH_MAIL) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  echo builtin (ASH_ECHO) [Y/n] y\r\n  printf builtin (ASH_PRINTF) [Y/n] y\r\n  test builtin (ASH_TEST) [Y/n] y\r\n  help builtin (ASH_HELP) [Y/n] y\r\n  getopts builtin (ASH_GETOPTS) [Y/n] y\r\n"]
[4.611556, "o", "  command builtin (ASH_CMDCMD) [Y/n/?] y\r\ncttyhack (2.7 kb) (CTTYHACK) [Y/n/?] y\r\nhush (70 kb) (HUSH) [Y/n/?] y\r\nInternal shell for embedded script support (SHELL_HUSH) [Y] y\r\n  Faster, but larger code (HUSH_NEED_FOR_SPEED) [Y/n] y\r\n"]
[4.611663, "o", "  bash-compatible extensions (HUSH_BASH_COMPAT) [Y/n] y\r\n    Brace expansion (HUSH_BRACE_EXPANSION) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    'source' and '.' builtins search current directory after $PATH (HUSH_BASH_SOURCE_CURDIR) [N/y/?] n\r\n  $LINENO variable (bashism) (HUSH_LINENO_VAR) [Y/n] y\r\n  Interactive mode (HUSH_INTERACTIVE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    Save command history to .hush_history (HUSH_SAVEHISTORY) [Y/n] y\r\n    Job control (HUSH_JOB) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support command substitution (HUSH_TICK) [Y/n/?] y\r\n"]
[4.611726, "o", "  Support if/then/elif/else/fi (HUSH_IF) [Y/n] y\r\n  Support for, while and until loops (HUSH_LOOPS) [Y/n] y\r\n  Support case ... esac statement (HUSH_CASE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support aliases (HUSH_ALIAS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support funcname() { commands; } syntax (HUSH_FUNCTIONS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    Support function keyword (HUSH_FUNCTION_KEYWORD) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    local builtin (HUSH_LOCAL) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Pseudorandom generator and $RANDOM variable (HUSH_RANDOM_SUPPORT) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support 'hush -x' option and 'set -x' command (HUSH_MODE_X) [Y/n/?] y\r\n"]
[4.611812, "o", "  echo builtin (HUSH_ECHO) [Y/n] y\r\n  printf builtin (HUSH_PRINTF) [Y/n] y\r\n  test builtin (HUSH_TEST) [Y/n] y\r\n  help builtin (HUSH_HELP) [Y/n] y\r\n  export builtin (HUSH_EXPORT) [Y/n] y\r\n    Support 'export -n' option (HUSH_EXPORT_N) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  readonly builtin (HUSH_READONLY) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  kill builtin (supports kill %jobspec) (HUSH_KILL) [Y/n] y\r\n  wait builtin (HUSH_WAIT) [Y/n] y\r\n  command builtin (HUSH_COMMAND) [Y/n] y\r\n  trap builtin (HUSH_TRAP) [Y/n] y\r\n  type builtin (HUSH_TYPE) [Y/n] y\r\n  times builtin (HUSH_TIMES) [Y/n] y\r\n  read builtin (HUSH_READ) [Y/n] y\r\n  set builtin (HUSH_SET) [Y/n] y\r\n  unset builtin (HUSH_UNSET) [Y/n] y\r\n  ulimit builtin (HUSH_ULIMIT) [Y/n] y\r\n  umask builtin (HUSH_UMASK) [Y/n] y\r\n  getopts builtin (HUSH_GETOPTS) [Y/n] y\r\n  memleak builtin (debugging) (HUSH_MEMLEAK) [N/y] n\r\n*\r\n* Options common to all shells\r\n*\r\n"]
[4.611832, "o", "POSIX math support (FEATURE_SH_MATH) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Extend POSIX math support to 64 bit (FEATURE_SH_MATH_64) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support BASE#nnnn literals (FEATURE_SH_MATH_BASE) [Y/n] y\r\nHide message on interactive shell startup (FEATURE_SH_EXTRA_QUIET) [Y/n/?] y\r\nStandalone shell (FEATURE_SH_STANDALONE) [N/y/?] n\r\nRun 'nofork' applets directly (FEATURE_SH_NOFORK) [N/y/?] n\r\nread -t N.NNN support (+110 bytes) (FEATURE_SH_READ_FRAC) [Y/n/?] y\r\nUse $HISTFILESIZE (FEATURE_SH_HISTFILESIZE) [Y/n/?] y\r\nEmbed scripts in the binary (FEATURE_SH_EMBEDDED_SCRIPTS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n*\r\n* System Logging Utilities\r\n*\r\n"]
[4.611903, "o", "klogd (6.2 kb) (KLOGD) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  *\r\n  * klogd should not be used together with syslog to kernel printk buffer\r\n  *\r\n"]
[4.612043, "o", "  Use the klogctl() interface (FEATURE_KLOGD_KLOGCTL) [Y/n/?] y\r\nlogger (6.5 kb) (LOGGER) [Y/n/?] y\r\nlogread (5 kb) (LOGREAD) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Double buffering (FEATURE_LOGREAD_REDUCED_LOCKING) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsyslogd (14 kb) (SYSLOGD) [Y/n/?] y\r\n"]
[4.612132, "o", "  Rotate message files (FEATURE_ROTATE_LOGFILE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Remote Log support (FEATURE_REMOTE_LOG) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support -D (drop dups) option (FEATURE_SYSLOGD_DUP) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support syslog.conf (FEATURE_SYSLOGD_CFG) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Include milliseconds in timestamps (FEATURE_SYSLOGD_PRECISE_TIMESTAMPS) [N/y/?] n\r\n  Read buffer size in bytes (FEATURE_SYSLOGD_READ_BUFFER_SIZE) [256] 256\r\n  Circular Buffer support (FEATURE_IPC_SYSLOG) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    Circular buffer size in Kbytes (minimum 4KB) (FEATURE_IPC_SYSLOG_BUFFER_SIZE) [16] 16\r\n  Linux kernel printk buffer support (FEATURE_KMSG_SYSLOG) [Y/n/?] y\r\n"]
